#: ../../source/validation/report/file-methodology.rst:3
msgid "By file — under which methodology"
msgstr "Per file — sotto quale metodologia"

#: ../../source/validation/report/file-methodology.rst:5
msgid ""
"The same view as ``freeports-validate who-grants -m <file>``, asked of the whole "
"repository at once instead of about the one file, contributor or methodology you "
"would name on the command line."
msgstr ""
"La stessa vista di ``freeports-validate who-grants -m <file>``, chiesta all'intero "
"repository in una volta anziché sul singolo file, contributore o metodologia che "
"nomineresti sulla riga di comando."

#: ../../source/validation/report/file-methodology.rst:11
msgid "**By file, listing the methodologies it was granted under**"
msgstr "**Per file, elencando le metodologie sotto cui è stato attestato**"

#: ../../source/validation/report/file-methodology.rst:13
msgid ""
"The same view as ``freeports-validate who-grants -m <file>``, for the whole "
"repository at once."
msgstr ""
"La stessa vista di ``freeports-validate who-grants -m <file>``, per l'intero "
"repository in una volta."

#: ../../source/validation/report/file-methodology.rst:15
msgid ""
"1 grant by 1 contributor under 1 methodology; coverage 1/1 (100%); check-grants: "
"passing"
msgstr ""
"1 attestazione di 1 contributore sotto 1 metodologia; copertura 1/1 (100%); check-"
"grants: passing"

#: ../../source/validation/report/file-methodology.rst:17
msgid ""
"*Generated by `freeports-validate report`, and demonstrative: it shows what this "
"repository's validation documents claim as of one run, not that the data is correct. "
"To be sure of any line, run `freeports-validate check-grants` yourself.* `What these "
"claims are worth: the general methodology "
"<https://docs.freeports.org/en/stable/validation/general_methodology.html>`_."
msgstr ""
"*Generata da `freeports-validate report`, e dimostrativa: mostra ciò che i documenti "
"di validazione di questo repository affermano al momento di una certa esecuzione, non"
" che i dati siano corretti. Per essere certo di una qualsiasi riga, esegui tu stesso "
"`freeports-validate check-grants`.* `Quanto valgano queste affermazioni: la "
"metodologia generale "
"<https://docs.freeports.org/en/stable/validation/general_methodology.html>`_."

